WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.580
- One, two three,

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.971
- We love Asian food!

00:00:06.971 --> 00:00:08.090
(laughing)

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.260
- We're playing would you
rather with Asian food.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.220
It's gonna be really hard
because I like all of it.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.160
- Tasty, tasty.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.700
Would you rather have Thai tea

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.980
or Vietnamese coffee?

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.640
- This is too hard already.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.590
Thai tea.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.420
Vietnamese iced coffee is very good also,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.440
but I would pick Thai tea.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.130
- I would probably pick Vietnamese coffee

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.850
just because I really love coffee.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.790
My teeth are so sensitive.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.410
Sometimes the Thai tea hurts my teeth.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.380
- Because it's cold?

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.213
- Yeah.

00:00:31.213 --> 00:00:32.695
- But so is Vietnamese iced coffee.

00:00:32.695 --> 00:00:35.365
So is any iced beverage.

00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:37.133
- Oh, it's iced coffee.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.020
(laughing)

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.960
Oh, well then, I guess,
honestly, just the hot version

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.443
of either of these.

00:00:42.443 --> 00:00:43.276
Yeah.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.300
- Jennifer.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.730
Would you rather eat

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.280
Thai fried rice or Kimchi fried rice?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.810
- Probably Kimchi fried
rice, if only because

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.780
the punch of Kimchi.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.613
Yeah, I love the punch.

00:00:52.613 --> 00:00:54.080
- I don't love the punch.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.380
I would go Thai with the
lime and the cilantro

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.030
and the herbs.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.970
- Would you rather eat Pho or Ramen?

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:01.820
- Ramen.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.110
- I'd rather eat Pho.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:03.943
- What, really?

00:01:03.943 --> 00:01:05.660
- I don't wanna talk about this on camera.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.231
- Oh no!

00:01:07.231 --> 00:01:08.290
I mean, I love both.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.800
- Yeah, I like one of them.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.970
- You don't like Ramen?

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.160
Have you kept this a
secret in our relationship?

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.307
- I don't want people to know.

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:17.320
- For this reason?

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.520
- I don't dislike Ramen.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.240
I just generally, when it
comes to like noodle dishes

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.270
I prefer Udon and then

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.250
- I do like Udon.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.050
Would you rather Indian
curry or Japanese curry?

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.640
- I feel like Indian curry can
be like a little bit lighter.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.530
- And there's a lot of
variety in Indian curry.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.390
- There might be variety
in Japanese curry,

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.790
but I am really only familiar
with the comfort food version.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.180
You know, that's like
what I ate growing up.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.540
So, if I am sober, Indian curry

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.767
and if I'm drunk then Japanese curry.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:48.060
- That's good.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:48.893
- Yeah.

00:01:48.893 --> 00:01:49.890
- I'm never drunk.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.930
So, I'm always Indian curry.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.290
- Niki, would you rather
have Pad Thai or Chow Mein?

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.123
- Chow Mein.

00:01:55.123 --> 00:01:56.027
- Okay.

00:01:56.027 --> 00:01:57.220
(laughing)

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.330
- I'm Chinese!

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.480
There's nothing better than
like going to my parent's house

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.740
where my grandma lives and being like,

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.930
"Grandma, can you make me noodles?"

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.940
and most of the time she
will fry up some Chow Mein.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.380
I do love Pad Thai.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.340
It's more tangy because
of the lime and the spices

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.490
and the Chow Mein is just I feel it.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:13.800
- I really like both.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.720
I feel like I had Chow Mein last night

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.090
and now I really want Pad Thai.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.340
So, Pad Thai.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.209
- Would you rather Bibimbap or Biryani?

00:02:22.209 --> 00:02:24.510
- Oh.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.290
I would rather have Biryani.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.390
- I'd pick Bibimbap.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.870
- I feel like there's usually like

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.100
some crispiness to the meat going on there

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.210
and I just really love crispy meat.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.570
Bibimbap is also really good.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.770
- I like Bibimbap a lot.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.150
- I like everything you've said to me.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.040
- I know.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.180
Me too.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.190
Also, the rice is crispy in Bibimbap

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:44.590
and you like dig it up from the bottom

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.970
cause the stone bowl is
hot and everything's hot

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.940
and it stays hot and you mix it all

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.360
and it's really good.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.420
The egg.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.253
Love a egg.

00:02:52.253 --> 00:02:54.970
- Would you rather have mango
sticky rice or Halo-Halo?

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.080
- Mango sticky rice.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.120
The rice is warm.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.930
The mango is refreshing.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:00.420
You mix it together.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:01.620
It's amazing.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.690
Halo-Halo is good.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.840
I think I also just didn't eat
that much of it growing up.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.020
- I prefer Halo-Halo.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.120
I just like the texture
a little bit better.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.230
I just like, it kinda reminds me of like

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.550
a whisper of ice cream.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.810
- I thought you don't like cold
things cause of your teeth.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.240
- I mean, I just don't like my teeth.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.073
- Okay.

00:03:17.073 --> 00:03:18.700
- Well, this game was revealing in that

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.560
it revealed that Asian cultures

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.760
have some really delicious food,

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.940
which we already knew.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:26.720
- It's like asking me
which child is my favorite.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.500
I love all of my children.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.650
I don't have children,

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.920
but the argument stands.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.753
- Yeah.

00:03:32.753 --> 00:03:35.540
And of my children, I love Ramen the most.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.610
- Jen, it's fine if you don't like Ramen.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.770
- I love it so.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.110
- I stand by what I said earlier.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.280
I think Asian people have
really done it the best.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.300
- Yeah.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.068
- That's just what I think.

00:03:47.068 --> 00:03:49.651
(groovy music)

